# A formal Russian letter: Обращаюсь к Вам с просьбой
subtitle: "Обращаюсь к Вам с просьбой: the set phrases of a formal Russian letter, the capital Вы, and the participles and gerunds that letters use — as Tom asks his landlady for permission."
tags: ["russian","formal letter","russian writing","official russian","russian phrases"]
teaches: ["writing/formal-letters","phrases/formal-register","grammar/participles"]
thumb: "band \"Write a formal letter in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Little kitchen in Russian: diminutives -ик, -очка, -онька","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/208-russian-little-kitchen.cast"}

## A formal Russian letter: Обращаюсь к Вам с просьбой
